<h2>Interaction Modes</h2>

<h3>Button variant</h3>

<p>The component renders a built-in styled button (blue background, white text, <code>12px 24px</code> padding by default). Customize appearance with the <code>buttonStyle</code> property using inline CSS:</p>

<pre><code class="language-css">background-color: #111827; color: white; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 20px; font-weight: 600;</code></pre>

<h3>Slot variant</h3>

<p>Set <code>variant</code> to <code>Slot</code> and design any Webflow element inside the slot — a button, banner, card, or link. The entire slot area becomes clickable and triggers the vCard download. This gives you full control over the trigger's appearance using Webflow's native design tools.</p>

<h2>Generated vCard Format</h2>

<p>The component outputs a vCard 3.0 file. Only fields with non-empty values are included:</p>

<pre><code>BEGIN:VCARD
VERSION:3.0
N:Smith;John;;;
FN:John Smith
ORG:Acme Corp
TITLE:Product Manager
TEL;TYPE=CELL:+1 555 000 0001
TEL;TYPE=WORK,VOICE:+1 555 000 0002
EMAIL;TYPE=WORK:john@acme.com
EMAIL:john@personal.com
ADR;TYPE=WORK:;;123 Main St;Springfield;IL;62701;USA
URL:https://john.example.com
NOTE:Met at conference 2024
END:VCARD</code></pre>

<h3>vCard Field Mapping</h3>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>vCard Field</th><th>Type Tag</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>firstName</code> + <code>lastName</code></td><td><code>N</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>fullName</code></td><td><code>FN</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>organization</code></td><td><code>ORG</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>title</code></td><td><code>TITLE</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>cellPhone</code></td><td><code>TEL</code></td><td><code>CELL</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>workPhone</code></td><td><code>TEL</code></td><td><code>WORK,VOICE</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>email</code></td><td><code>EMAIL</code></td><td><code>WORK</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>additionalEmail</code></td><td><code>EMAIL</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>streetAddress</code> + <code>city</code> + <code>state</code> + <code>postalCode</code> + <code>country</code></td><td><code>ADR</code></td><td><code>WORK</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>websiteUrl</code></td><td><code>URL</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>note</code></td><td><code>NOTE</code></td><td>—</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Download Behavior</h2>

<p>The component creates a <code>Blob</code> with the vCard content and type <code>text/vcard</code>, generates a temporary object URL, triggers the browser download dialog, then immediately revokes the URL. No server-side processing is required.</p>

<h2>CMS Binding</h2>

<p>Bind any contact field to a CMS field for dynamic contact pages. Useful patterns:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Employee directory: bind all fields to a Staff CMS collection</li>
  <li>Speaker listing: bind name, title, organization, and email</li>
  <li>Contact page: use a single-item CMS collection as a data source</li>
</ul>

<h2>Future Plans</h2>

<ul>
  <li>QR code option for sharing the vCard without downloading</li>
</ul>
